{
 "id": "world_affordances",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "GENERAL BASE AFFORDANCE VOCABULARY (block 280000). A world provides AFFORDANCES (admissible actions) + observations; the agent's decision COLLAPSES over the afforded set. The 8-type minimal basis (move, extract_resource, transform, transfer, communicate, ingest, rest, harm) spans all six effect classes (position/existence/configuration/possession/information/vital) x targets, grounded in AFFORDANCE_VOCABULARY_SCIENCE.md (Gibson affordance taxonomy; NSM/Jackendoff/VerbNet action primitives; Mauss gift-vs-trade; Spelke/Hamlin core-knowledge help-vs-harm). Each ActionType is a STRIPS schema: precondition (=affordance condition) + effect (=world rewrite) + base_weight (=collapse prior). PROVISION rules set impulse=base_weight ONLY when the precondition holds (else 0 -> the decision core prunes it, never scored), so 'the world provides the afforded subset' is purely additive over the block-279000 decision core -- NO decision-core change. `harm` is a MEMBER of the basis, offered ONLY when a target is in range (precondition-gated, not permanently on the menu), at a LOW base prior -- representable so a norm against it is representable, but rarely afforded and rarely selected. EFFECT rules perform the STRIPS rewrite once the agent commits. ZERO new Rust (composes existing DSL Terms + add_node/add_edge/del_edge/set_attr). self_load_only.",
